From 3dcbfb3a17fb1eb15d0193915ed1771ccb46a146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 16:51:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/98] procfs: implement /proc/<pid>/maps (Linux-compatible
 address-space dump)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a "maps" file to each /proc/<pid> directory listing the process's
vm_map_entry regions, one per line:

  <start>-<end> <perms> <offset> <dev> <inode> <pathname>
  00362000-0038c000 rwxp 00000000 00:00 1215 libXfont.so.1.4.1

Walks p->vm_map under vm_map_lock_read.  perms come from the entry's
VM_PROT_* bits; the pathname/inode are the backing file's basename and
inode.  Crucially, every ld.so library segment is a MAP_PRIVATE mapping,
which substrate represents as an anonymous COW shadow over the
VM_OBJ_TYPE_VNODE object — so we walk the ->shadow chain down to the
vnode object to recover the real backing file (otherwise every library
line is blank, as a first cut of this showed).  dev is a 00:00
placeholder (substrate has no dev numbers here).

This is what lets a faulting userspace EIP (e.g. from the kernel `trap`
flag's TRAP line) be mapped back to library + offset for addr2line —
previously impossible, which blocked debugging the dtcm/libXfont crash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/fs/procfs.c | 109 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 107 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/fs/procfs.c b/sys/fs/procfs.c
index 2838338e..274a8831 100644
--- a/sys/fs/procfs.c
+++ b/sys/fs/procfs.c
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <vm/vm_kmem.h>
 #include <vm/vm_page.h>
+#include <vm/vm_map.h>
